# OpenClaw — MCP Registry Domain

## Purpose

Second-party validator + registry for MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers. Every
MCP submitted to the registry runs through an L0-L4 governance gate before it can
be surfaced for install by a tenant. Certified entries are safe-installable;
conditional entries surface reviewer notes; failed entries are blocked from install.

The reason this domain exists: **Anthropic authored the MCP spec but does not run a
third-party validator for MCP servers.** OpenClaw is the neutral trust surface. See
`/mnt/results/openclaw-moat-v2/02-moat-and-pitch.md` §2.3.

## What this domain IS

- Manifest ingestion + L0-L4 gate scoring (in-process, inspection-only)
- Registry storage — one row per MCP, versioned per submission
- Tenant install join via `tenant_mcps` (workspace-scoped)
- Human reviewer L4 sign-off endpoint

## What this domain is NOT

- NOT a live MCP runtime. Live invocation happens in the per-tenant runtime with the pinned version. See `MDC_architecture.md` for runtime topology.
- NOT a package manager. The registry stores the manifest, not the code. Entrypoints resolve at install time.
- NOT an Anthropic-owned surface. OpenClaw is deliberately neutral so both first- and third-party MCPs can be catalogued.

## Backend

```
artifacts/api-server/
├── src/lib/mcps/
│   ├── validator.ts    # L0-L4 gate scoring
│   └── registry.ts     # in-memory + seed-file backed, DB-ready
├── src/routes/mcps.ts  # 6 endpoints, mounted at /api/mcps/*
└── corpus/mcps/
    └── seed.json       # 7 reference MCPs (5 Anthropic + 2 OpenClaw first-party)

lib/db/src/schema/
├── mcps.ts             # registry table
├── mcpVersions.ts      # per-submission versioning
├── mcpBenchmarks.ts    # gate reports over time
└── tenantMcps.ts       # tenant install join
```

## HTTP contract

| Method | Path | Auth | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/mcps/health` | public | Registry health + seed path |
| GET | `/api/mcps` | public | List (filter: `category`, `gateStatus`) |
| GET | `/api/mcps/:slug` | public | Single MCP w/ gate report |
| POST | `/api/mcps/register` | public | Submit manifest, get gate report |
| POST | `/api/mcps/:slug/certify` | reviewer | L4 sign-off (sets grade=CERTIFIED) |
| POST | `/api/mcps/:slug/install` | tenant | Install into workspace (refused if FAILED) |
| GET | `/api/mcps/:slug/gate` | public | Latest gate report |

**Auth boundary (this branch):** `/register` is currently public so external
submitters can propose without an account. `certify` + `install` need to be
gated by `requireWorkspaceMember` before merge — flagged in
`docs/audits/2026-07-agent-robustness/06-mcp-domain.md`.

## Gate levels

| Level | What it checks | Auto-pass? | Weight |
|---|---|---|---|
| L0 | Manifest sanity (slug, transport, entrypoint, tools declared) | yes | 30 |
| L1 | Tool schema conformance (name, input_schema present) | yes | 20 |
| L2 | Privilege honesty (no wildcard net/fs/env) | yes | 20 |
| L3 | Adversarial (name/description red-flag regex) | yes | 20 |
| L4 | Human reviewer sign-off | **no** | 10 |

- Overall score 0-100. Grade cutoffs: <40 FAILED, 40-64 CONDITIONAL, 65+ CONDITIONAL (until L4), CERTIFIED once L4 passes.
- Every submission bumps `currentVersion` on the row. Rollbacks re-point currentVersion at an older `mcp_versions` row.

## What NOT to do

- Do NOT run the MCP server in-process from the validator. Inspection-only.
- Do NOT accept a `--dangerous` opt-out to skip the gate. The gate is the point.
- Do NOT extend the validator to run adversarial prompts *against* the MCP — that requires a per-MCP sandbox and belongs in the MCP training loop (`.cursor/rules/13-mcp-training.mdc`).
- Do NOT store secrets in `declaredPrivileges.env`. Only env *keys* should be listed. Values live in `tenant_connectors.encrypted_credentials`.

## Corpus provenance

Seed file at `corpus/mcps/seed.json`. Contains 7 reference MCPs:
- 5 Anthropic official (`filesystem`, `postgres`, `git`, `github`, `slack`)
- 2 OpenClaw first-party (`openclaw-legal`, `openclaw-robustness`)

When the DB schema tables are migrated (via `drizzle migrate`), the seed
propagates into the `mcps` + `mcp_versions` tables. Until then, the registry
loads from the seed file only.
